report:
Two problems would block sending this to referees, so the verdict is not ok.

**What I checked.** I read s1 to s7, the Online Appendix and PLANO-CORRECAO. I recomputed the headline arithmetic against the paper's own tables and found nothing wrong:
- shares of R (2.2, 8.8, 15.3, 62.7 and 42.1 per cent);
- the differences, ratios and relative percentages for H3 to H21b (307.9, 48.9, 30.2, 22.2, 68.0/96.2 and 64.9);
- the operating-point ranges in Table C11 (0.37 to 0.46, 0.47 to 0.66, 0.01 to 0.08, and the threshold 0.40 in 7 of 14 combinations);
- the camera geometry (field of view 63.96 degrees gives a ground width of 1.249 times the altitude; GSDs of 4.88, 2.44 and 1.14 cm per pixel);
- the tile and instance counts (1,106 tiles, 4,678 boxes, 18,858 persons).

The Liao Table 5 values (50.2 against 74.5) match the conferred note in `04-bibliografia`. The new PAR, ACM and EU references are in s8.

**Reviewer 1's points (PLANO-CORRECAO).** E1 to E3, M1 to M5, S1 to S8, C1, C3, C4, A2, A3 and B1 are answered. C2 is not, because of the placeholders below. E1 is also slightly breached by the result added to 4.7.

**Blocking 1.** The verdict "not demonstrated" and "Claim supported: None" still rest on no stated standard. Earlier MAJOR 2b asked for one; the integration pass instead added the cut-points 0.09 (object rate) and 0.42 (armed recall). Table C11 shows these sit just outside observed points: Twin-75 seed 2 on held-out frames has object rate 0.097 at recall 0.420. A referee will read them as chosen after the fact. The fix is to declare a standard set after the results (object rate at or below 0.10 with armed recall and precision both above one half) and to report the best observed point, recall 0.42 at precision 0.61. Exact edits for 4.7, 5.4, 6.1, Table declaracao and s7 are in the major list.

**Blocking 2.** The Declarations still contain the bracketed author instructions for Ethics and Conflict of interest. There is no dual-use statement, and decision A5 (the co-author's name, affiliation and conflict of interest) is open. The link to the Civil Police and the police survey imagery makes a full conflict-of-interest statement essential.

**Length.** The JMIS build is 55 pages against 50: required before a JMIS submission, but not a block. Moving two figures to the appendix, one source per fact in 3.1 and about 400 words of cuts should reach 50.

**Other minor items** (exact text in the minor list):
- abstract: an unsupported "rarely state" claim, the armed-category premise stated as fact, 25 to be written as 25.3, and "ceiling" used for a model trained on 1,106 images;
- recall and mAP50 conflated in the illumination results (5.5 and 6.3);
- an over-broad claim that no aerial benchmark reports results by light, against DroneCrowd and UAVDT;
- the first sentence of 3.1 against Appendix A1;
- an unresolvable label beside an interval that excludes zero (5.4);
- the hypotheses table cited out of order;
- "most" where only a ratio supports it;
- appendix leftovers from the revision history.

